(6883323, 1036626, 67152, '<td valign="top">A wonderful moment, a beautiful family.   Trying to figure out why it scored where it did...maybe the crop?  It almost seems that a more square crop with the baby and Mom at opposite corners may have been more conventional and scored better.  But personally, I like the lines on the left and the tree over Mom''s head on the right.  Well done.</td>', 'A wonderful moment, a beautiful family.   Trying to figure out why it scored where it did...maybe the crop?  It almost seems that a more square crop with the baby and Mom at opposite corners may have been more conventional and scored better.  But personally, I like the lines on the left and the tree over Mom''s head on the right.  Well done.', '2012-10-15 08:10:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6883329, 1036588, 104230, '<td valign="top">Congratulations John.  Very poignant, especially after seeing the other shot.  Another excellent capture.</td>', 'Congratulations John.  Very poignant, especially after seeing the other shot.  Another excellent capture.', '2012-10-15 08:43:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6883333, 1036626, 109387, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i> A wonderful moment, a beautiful family.   Trying to figure out why it scored where it did...maybe the crop?  It almost seems that a more square crop with the baby and Mom at opposite corners may have been more conventional and scored better.  But personally, I like the lines on the left and the tree over Mom''s head on the right.  Well done. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Maybe it didn''t get a better score because some people could see it as a sort of snapshot. It''s not a snapshot because I had the challenge title in mind but I didn''t sacrifice our beautiful day for a more studied shot. You''re right, the crop was the main issue: I had to crop on the right because of an electricity pole right behind her. The square crop is something I almost never use, and i liked the lines in the left as well.</td>', 'Originally posted by bassbone: A wonderful moment, a beautiful family.   Trying to figure out why it scored where it did...maybe the crop?  It almost seems that a more square crop with the baby and Mom at opposite corners may have been more conventional and scored better.  But personally, I like the lines on the left and the tree over Mom''s head on the right.  Well done.   Maybe it didn''t get a better score because some people could see it as a sort of snapshot. It''s not a snapshot because I had the challenge title in mind but I didn''t sacrifice our beautiful day for a more studied shot. You''re right, the crop was the main issue: I had to crop on the right because of an electricity pole right behind her. The square crop is something I almost never use, and i liked the lines in the left as well.', '2012-10-15 08:56:17.000000', NULL, 0),
