(6883582, 1036651, 41337, '<td valign="top">Two things jump out at me.<br/> <br/>1) It''s not a stream so it''s already starting to seem like a shoehorn. <br/> <br/>2) Composition. It''s very strange. On one hand you have the tree line sloping downward, but the water itself appears to be flowing upward from right to left, settling in the center. I''m not sure what the thinking was here, but I don''t get a sense of the down stream effect at all. As a result I''m left with the notion that perhaps you failed at trying to get the shot you really wanted and had to settle for this instead. Now technically this probably shouldn''t matter, but I do think voters in general let these sorts of feelings affect their vote. I can say without hesitation that it does for me. If I get the sense that the photographer had to settle for something less than ideal then it affects my vote. I didn''t vote in this challenge but I''m guessing had I did I probably would have given it a 6 (mostly due to the exposure/processing).</td>', 'Two things jump out at me. 1) It''s not a stream so it''s already starting to seem like a shoehorn.  2) Composition. It''s very strange. On one hand you have the tree line sloping downward, but the water itself appears to be flowing upward from right to left, settling in the center. I''m not sure what the thinking was here, but I don''t get a sense of the down stream effect at all. As a result I''m left with the notion that perhaps you failed at trying to get the shot you really wanted and had to settle for this instead. Now technically this probably shouldn''t matter, but I do think voters in general let these sorts of feelings affect their vote. I can say without hesitation that it does for me. If I get the sense that the photographer had to settle for something less than ideal then it affects my vote. I didn''t vote in this challenge but I''m guessing had I did I probably would have given it a 6 (mostly due to the exposure/processing).', '2012-10-15 15:10:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6883588, 1036721, 10785, '<td valign="top">Precious!!</td>', 'Precious!!', '2012-10-15 15:24:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6883601, 1036523, 110930, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Peter ~ Well-deserved win! Love the title. Fantastic capture. You really rock that lens. Love your sports photography.</td>', 'Congrats, Peter ~ Well-deserved win! Love the title. Fantastic capture. You really rock that lens. Love your sports photography.', '2012-10-15 15:37:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6883602, 1036728, 10785, '<td valign="top">No comments so I will add one for you.<br/> <br/>I honestly don''t feel this shot deserved such a low score. You have even lighting with no clipping of shadows though there are no major highglights. The model is pleasing and pleasant and her pose is good with the hand grabbing something a nice touch. You got good DoF and the tree adds interest with a nice line and acts as framing in the composition.  The technicals of the camera work are all good. Exposure, color, focus, DoF, composition... all good work.<br/> <br/>I can''t remember what you''re using for software, but the PP is a little lacking in contrast. Try to adjust your black point a touch lower and bring your whites up a touch more. You can do that by adjusting highlights and shadows or through a curves adjustment or even by levels. The shot may be a hair soft but it is a sharpness issue and not a focus issue. It could be brought up in PP.<br/> <br/>I would have voted this a 6 and I feel the score should be more in the 5.5 - 5.7 range.<br/> <br/>Well Done!</td>', 'No comments so I will add one for you. I honestly don''t feel this shot deserved such a low score. You have even lighting with no clipping of shadows though there are no major highglights. The model is pleasing and pleasant and her pose is good with the hand grabbing something a nice touch. You got good DoF and the tree adds interest with a nice line and acts as framing in the composition.  The technicals of the camera work are all good. Exposure, color, focus, DoF, composition... all good work. I can''t remember what you''re using for software, but the PP is a little lacking in contrast. Try to adjust your black point a touch lower and bring your whites up a touch more. You can do that by adjusting highlights and shadows or through a curves adjustment or even by levels. The shot may be a hair soft but it is a sharpness issue and not a focus issue. It could be brought up in PP. I would have voted this a 6 and I feel the score should be more in the 5.5 - 5.7 range. Well Done!', '2012-10-15 15:37:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6883623, 1036651, 137576, '<td valign="top">Re the stream maybe it''s a missed language but float down stream doesn''t mean a stream, stream is the flow the amazon flows down stream as does the Nile etc if the quote was float down the stream then I''d get it but it''s float down stream as in go with the flow???</td>', 'Re the stream maybe it''s a missed language but float down stream doesn''t mean a stream, stream is the flow the amazon flows down stream as does the Nile etc if the quote was float down the stream then I''d get it but it''s float down stream as in go with the flow???', '2012-10-15 16:17:51.000000', NULL, 0),
